      Swollen feet &amp; ankles are a condition that many seniors have and ignore…<br><br>

      Not good!<br><br>

      If you sit down, remove your socks &amp; shoes, and it looks as if there was a rubber band around your ankle or your socks are still &quot;there&quot;… listen up.<br><br>

      Do your feet occasionally swell or ache, even after you've tried everything to relieve the painful puffiness?<br><br>

      Like moving more regularly, drinking more water, or even wearing supportive shoes or compression socks…<br><br>

      This is not only frustrating, but it is unsightly.<br><br>

      The good news is - you can do something about it.<br><br>

      These symptoms may point to circulation issues, which cause blood and fluid to pool in the tissue around your feet and ankles.<br><br>

      Fortunately, researchers found that seniors with high levels of a little-known antarctic nutrient had significantly lowered blood-flow risks.<br><br>

